{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain","id":1142767,"title":"Can the Naming Art \"cure\" the Thallain?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-21T18:05:23-07:00","id":1142767,"title":"Can the Naming Art \"cure\" the Thallain?","content":"Given how the Naming Art can change a person's core nature, how about the changing the Thallain back into Kithain? I also don't have the book, so any details about whether or not Unleashings could aid in this would be much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T18:28:14-07:00","id":1142776,"title":"","content":"A Strict reading of the rules would say no, it is well beyond the limits placed on level 5 and unleashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T18:48:53-07:00","id":1142780,"title":"","content":"Nothing could turn them &quot;Back&quot; into Kithain, they, last I checked were never kithain in the first place.<br /> <br /> it MIGHT be a cool plot point though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T20:19:33-07:00","id":1142799,"title":"","content":"There's nothing to 'cure.' The Fae are creatures of dreams, and there are both good dreams and bad dreams.<br /> <br /> If anybody needs to be cured, it's humanity itself for dreaming up these horrors in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T21:18:00-07:00","id":1142808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1142799#post1142799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anybody needs to be cured, it's humanity itself for dreaming up these horrors in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. Have fun trying to tell humanity to stop having nightmares and being afraid of stuff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T01:12:54-07:00","id":1142835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1142808#post1142808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean. Have fun trying to tell humanity to stop having nightmares and being afraid of stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought that's what the Technocracy was trying to do in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T07:31:18-07:00","id":1142897,"title":"","content":"In 2e? Sure. Why not? In 2e, Thallain were corrupt, &quot;broken&quot; Kithain.<br /> C20? Not so much. In C20, Thallain were created by the Fomorians &quot;as-is&quot;. You can't &quot;cure&quot; them any more than Naming could &quot;cure&quot; a sidhe into a boggan or a pooka into a troll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T07:43:11-07:00","id":1142900,"title":"","content":"Can I ask some general naming Questions?<br /> <br /> when a buildings purpose is changed with naming, is it retroactively changed?<br /> <br /> or do things to do with the new purpose just drift its way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T08:34:38-07:00","id":1142915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1142897#post1142897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e? Sure. Why not? In 2e, Thallain were corrupt, &quot;broken&quot; Kithain.<br /> C20? Not so much. In C20, Thallain were created by the Fomorians &quot;as-is&quot;. You can't &quot;cure&quot; them any more than Naming could &quot;cure&quot; a sidhe into a boggan or a pooka into a troll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> However there is a Thallain in c20 that &quot;reproduces&quot; by transforming presained Kithain into more of its kind. Perhaps Naming would allow a Cure of this type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T08:36:28-07:00","id":1142917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1142915#post1142915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> However there is a Thallain in c20 that &amp;quot;reproduces&amp;quot; by transforming presained Kithain into more of its kind. Perhaps Naming would allow a Cure of this type.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes; the savartel. I'd agree with you, here, but only on savartel that would normally have been some other kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T10:20:59-07:00","id":1142957,"title":"","content":"I'd say, you could try, and under certain circumstances you could succeed, but otherwise you're tempting Fate to kick your ass, as was the case with 1,5-2e Naming. But it's less about &quot;curing&quot; and more about Vulgar Magick \u2013 forcing a reality to be a certain way \u2013 something Changelings doesn't appreciate all that much.<br /> <br /> Which might manifest as Undoing immediately, if you fail or botch, or some stern looking Norn ladies coming for you to make you never be seen again, if you succeed, soon afterwards.<br /> <br /> \u200b_________________\u200b_________________<br /> <b>P.S.</b> You can discuss your idea with your Storyteller and if it's possible, she may incorporate your into the campaign. Otherwise it's good practice to discuss soft and hard limits of high level magic between players and Storytellers to not make players feel having a useless abilities and not forcing Storytellers into situations, they have zero skills to deal with.<br /> <br /> As with time travel, unlimited transmutation spell might sound great on paper, but can be huge pain in the ass for a Storyteller and its gonna be your fault for forcing one of your co-players into situation she doesn't want to be in and GMing you a shitty story resolution or shutting down the campaign prematurely.<br /> <br /> Some Storytellers are the kind, who are ready for everything or at least try to be and ready for challenges. Others can be negotiated with (don't confuse with being persuaded or pressured). And some shouldn't be pushed into games, genres and situations they suck at at all costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 09-22-2017, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T17:36:06-07:00","id":1143094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1142915#post1142915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> However there is a Thallain in c20 that &amp;quot;reproduces&amp;quot; by transforming presained Kithain into more of its kind. Perhaps Naming would allow a Cure of this type.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if two can play at that game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T18:41:59-07:00","id":1143106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1143094#post1143094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if two can play at that game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its one of their KIth boons so its not like its an art they get. Its a unique quality of their dream trying to replicate it for symetries sake could I imagine more likely cause said changeling to be Undone.. and possibly the one trying it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T01:18:19-07:00","id":1144309,"title":"","content":"I've been toying with making a Korred character who has a way of reforming the Thallain as part of his Testament birthright. Figured it could just swap their primary and secondary legacies though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12635-tomofviledarkness","name":"TomOfVileDarkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T01:53:55-07:00","id":1144311,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you aren't really &quot;curing&quot; them.<br /> <br /> But Unleashings really don't have limit, as in they never really explained any to us... So I would say Legendary Uses of Naming may have been what created the Changeling Way Ritual. So at the very least you may be able to kill one, and maybe do some sort of Group Naming Unleashing to change it's souls Name into something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T07:00:55-07:00","id":1144386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TomOfVileDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1144309#post1144309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been toying with making a Korred character who has a way of reforming the Thallain as part of his Testament birthright. Figured it could just swap their primary and secondary legacies though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! I've been super curious to see what folks do with the Korred birthright <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T09:47:44-07:00","id":1144467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1144311#post1144311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you aren't really &quot;curing&quot; them.<br /> <br /> But Unleashings really don't have limit, as in they never really explained any to us... So I would say Legendary Uses of Naming may have been what created the Changeling Way Ritual. So at the very least you may be able to kill one, and maybe do some sort of Group Naming Unleashing to change it's souls Name into something else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unleashings have limits. Naming specifically covers what it can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T03:52:16-07:00","id":1145483,"title":"","content":"Could Banality &quot;cure&quot; the Thallain? Some Thallain's nature makes it incredibly hard to not be, well, a monster. Being turned into a normal human could seem a much better option. I had this vague idea of a well-meaning Ghast struggling against their nature and their kithain friends seeing no way to help them beyond this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mark Storey","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/555-marks4trying","name":"Marks4trying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar555_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T05:58:22-07:00","id":1145499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marks4trying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1145483#post1145483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Banality &amp;quot;cure&amp;quot; the Thallain? Some Thallain's nature makes it incredibly hard to not be, well, a monster. Being turned into a normal human could seem a much better option. I had this vague idea of a well-meaning Ghast struggling against their nature and their kithain friends seeing no way to help them beyond this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still isn't a cure it's more like &quot;mercy&quot; killing. Even though atleast it generally leaves the possibility of rebirth.<br /> <br /> But generally there is no cure for being a Thallain because being one is not a disease, curse or afliction. They are as much of the Dreaming as the Kithain are. They are just the other side of the coin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T08:34:34-07:00","id":1145535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1145499#post1145499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That still isn't a cure it's more like &quot;mercy&quot; killing. Even though atleast it generally leaves the possibility of rebirth.<br /> <br /> But generally there is no cure for being a Thallain because being one is not a disease, curse or afliction. They are as much of the Dreaming as the Kithain are. They are just the other side of the coin.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I absolutely see where you're coming from, but if it's a choice between stabbing a troubled eleven year old through the heart and sending them to a rather unpleasant reform school, the difference is pretty significant. I'm sort of assuming that this would be a prelude to an epic quest to find a True Cure. Of course, in a very dark campaign it might be a reminder that sometimes in the World of Darkness there are no good options...</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mark Storey","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/555-marks4trying","name":"Marks4trying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar555_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T09:37:43-07:00","id":1145551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marks4trying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1145535#post1145535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">epic quest to find a True Cure.</div> </div> </div> </div>But my point is ultimately that it is a fool's errand to search for a cure for Thallain equal to a quest to find a cure for being a Pooka or more accurately to cure the Kithain condition. Thallain are just as much part of the Dreaming as the Kithain are. Nightmares are not a disease but a natural part of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Naturally YMMV and you may run a chronicle about seeking such cure and it may be epic and glorious but to me the whole idea of curing someone who is completely healthy of his/her own basic nature just sounds wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T13:06:47-07:00","id":1145613,"title":"","content":"If Thallain is just another side of the coin, Kithain might invite Fomorians to rule over the Dreaming too. <br /> <br /> What could possibly<br /> <br /> Or, you know, you might consider, all the problems Kithain are facing today are the result of the Thuata de Dannan winning a war, that should've not been fought in the first place...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T13:39:55-07:00","id":1145622,"title":"","content":"Sure. Because being lorded over by embodied psychoses and infinitely powerful nightmare-inducing living hallucinations was <i>so</i> much better for Stone Age man.<br /> <br /> I loved the Guide to the Technocracy's intro. It put things into perspective, from a certain point of view. Sure, the Tuathans may have screwed over the Dreaming by choosing to withdraw from all possible perception...but life under the Fomorians was hell on earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T15:00:17-07:00","id":1145640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1145551#post1145551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But my point is ultimately that it is a fool's errand to search for a cure for Thallain equal to a quest to find a cure for being a Pooka or more accurately to cure the Kithain condition. Thallain are just as much part of the Dreaming as the Kithain are. Nightmares are not a disease but a natural part of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Naturally YMMV and you may run a chronicle about seeking such cure and it may be epic and glorious but to me the whole idea of curing someone who is completely healthy of his/her own basic nature just sounds wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;basic nature&quot; of a ghast makes it very hard for them to not murder people. If they don't eat internal body parts from dreamers or changelings every single week they start suffering damage from any sound louder than a whisper no matter the source. Unless they somehow live an incredibly controlled environment there's a good chance that this might kill them and certainly doesn't sound pleasant. Yes it's theoretically possible that somehow they can get hold of their particular dietary needs without murder but every single week without fail? Also it's not like everyone is fine with the idea of cannibalism anyway. Remember ghasts ,and Thallian in general, are changelings they have a human part as well as a fae part so that's part of their &quot;basic nature&quot; too. I can't see how the idea of trying to cure a ghast who hates what they are is so wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mark Storey","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/555-marks4trying","name":"Marks4trying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar555_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T16:36:08-07:00","id":1145660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1145622#post1145622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loved the Guide to the Technocracy's intro. It put things into perspective, from a certain point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shameless propaganda piece, definitely! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T17:05:30-07:00","id":1145670,"title":"","content":"That the Fomorians are unpleasant and their rule over men would be a horrible time to be one does not change the fact that they still are a very primordial part of the Dreaming. The Tuatha, I believe, understood this and that is part of the reason why Fomorians and the Thallain were imprisoned instead of fought to extinction. Another part could be that the Tuatha did not wish to risk casualties and further war when surrender was offered but that is beside the point.<br /> <br /> Yes you can justify fighting Nightmares and yes some might want a life without being one, just like some humans would prefer to be something else, but it doesn't mean that there is, nor should be, a cure to someones basic nature. Besides considering that Legacies are a mechanical way to portray ones personality and since the Nightmare Legacy is always dominant in Thallain, though they also have a Seelie or Unseelie secondary Legacy which represents their human half (C20 p.370), it is unlikely that they would come to hate their basic nature.<br /> <br /> But incase there is a &quot;cure&quot; that can change the basic nature of a Thallain then there should exist a &quot;cure&quot; for the Kithain condition. If one can twist a piece of Fomorian Dream into a Tuathan Dream, as I assume most of you mean cure as something that would change them into their Kithain counterparts, then there should be a way to untwist a piece of Tuathan Dream back into a piece of Fomorian Dream.<br /> <br /> And admittedly there is a precedent for this sort of thing in the Sevartal birthright, but even that is not a permanent change, but I like to think it more as an exception that enforces the rule. Naturally YMMV.<br /> <br /> But in the end I am the last person to restrict how you want to play the game, if you gain enjoyment from a plot where a repentant Thallain seeks to cure his &quot;condition&quot; then by all means do. I'm just not getting the whole point of view where we look at something different and immediately think it should be cured from being itself. The general point of Thallain is that they like to be themselves, hence even mechanically having unique primary Legacies to represent that, no matter how we humans see them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T06:49:05-07:00","id":1145780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1145670#post1145670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... But in the end I am the last person to restrict how you want to play the game, if you gain enjoyment from a plot where a repentant Thallain seeks to cure his &quot;condition&quot; then by all means do. I'm just not getting the whole point of view where we look at something different and immediately think it should be cured from being itself. The general point of Thallain is that they like to be themselves, hence even mechanically having unique primary Legacies to represent that, no matter how we humans see them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel this is looking at something different and thinking it has to be cured from being itself. I<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> tried to explain where I'm coming from and I'm not sure how to rephrase it. I think we'll end up in one of those endless circular debates if we go on. As </span></span></span>I think you hinted at this has a lot to do with what we each enjoy about the Thallain. At the end of the day I don't want to restrict how you play the game either.<br /> <br /> YMMV<br /> <br /> Best Wishes using the Thallain as you see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mark Storey","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/555-marks4trying","name":"Marks4trying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar555_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T05:17:10-07:00","id":1146029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1145613#post1145613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Thallain is just another side of the coin, Kithain might invite Fomorians to rule over the Dreaming too.<br /> <br /> What could possibly<br /> <br /> Or, you know, you might consider, all the problems Kithain are facing today are the result of the Thuata de Dannan winning a war, that should've not been fought in the first place...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah! They had no place entering World War II!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T11:39:49-07:00","id":1146111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1146029#post1146029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah! They had no place entering World War II!</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Is there some some connection between <i>Thuata de Dannan </i>and World War 2 I am missing? <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 10-02-2017, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T16:21:37-07:00","id":1146185,"title":"","content":"There's a reason humanity turned towards banality, people try to pin it all on the Technocracy but they have a reasonable argument. Safety is worth wonder. We don't need unicorns if we get rid of the monsters. The price of the Dreaming is horrors and its price apparently humanity doesn't want to pay.<br /> <br /> The counterpoint seems to be &quot;you're going to pay it anyway&quot; since the Formorians don't seem to be effected all that much By Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T18:33:04-07:00","id":1146210,"title":"","content":"10 successes in Naming 5 can permanently turn a werewolf into a puppy. With that many (and I'm not sure it would even take that many, but the examples are over the place) could certainly change a target's kith. So you could turn a bogart into a boggan, but you could also use it to turn a boggan into a sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T23:27:38-07:00","id":1146264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1146111#post1146111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Is there some some connection between <i>Thuata de Dannan </i>and World War 2 I am missing? <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sorry I must have confused them with Dwight K. Shrute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.hark.com/clips/hpfrshkvjg-typical-american-arrogance\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.hark.com/clips/hpfrshkvjg-typical-american-arrogance\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.hark.com/clips/hpfrshkvjg-typical-american-arrogance\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.hark.com/clips/hpfrshkvjg-typical-american-arrogance </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T15:40:22-07:00","id":1146464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142767-can-the-naming-art-cure-the-thallain?p=1146210#post1146210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> <